/-!
# Rigid arithmetic of cuts

How the exact statement `N(x) = ⌊x⌋` constrains the zeros of `ζ`, by operations that have no sign and are not linear
floor identities: the cut system and its kernel, nonlinear ledgers, effective recurrence, the metric geometry of Beurling
systems, and the extremal position of the zero of maximal angle.
-/
